From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:40:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] editor heights: derived data (normal map, tier error grids)
 is refreshed over the changed rectangle grown by 2 samples (PadDirtyRect), no
 SyncTerrain queue entry that copies old sim heights over the view

- UpdateError got the tight rectangle: the error cells that share a corner sample with the edit were skipped on every side (model: missed in 92% of random edits).
- NotifyMapChange queued a dirty rectangle that SyncTerrain later copies out of the sim field over the view field; the sim field only gets the edit at its next beat.
  The sink now calls UpdateNormalMap directly once the terrain is finalized.
- The same padded rectangle is used for the sim field's error grids (ApplyPendingHeightEdits).
- EdDirtyRectTest: the pure function and models of the engine's UpdateNormalMap / UpdateErrorKernel loops.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F37er45a7etRuMgEW1q3kY

